#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124287 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124475 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "74f126da-5f3b-5af8-9aee-d6f0a4c61c49" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Shape of a Level Curve"}] :question/id #uuid "5791bd77-96c7-571d-b8b5-76cb62eb0a9d" :question/math-academy-id "e-4228" :question/problem "The level curves of the function $f(x,y) = \\dfrac{x^2+2y^2-2}{x^2}$ are given by $f(x,y) = c.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $c=1$ gives a circle\n\nII. $c=0$ gives an ellipse\n\nIII. $c=2$ gives a hyperbola" :question/worked-solution "Setting $f(x,y) = c$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}-2}{{x}^{2}} & =c \\\\ {x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}-2 & =c{x}^{2} \\\\ (1-c){x}^{2}+2{y}^{2} & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore:\n\n- If $c = 1,$ then the level curve is $y^2 = 1,$ which consists of two lines.\n\n- If $c = 0,$ then the level curve is $x^2+2y^2=2,$ which is an ellipse.\n\n- If $c = 2,$ then the level curve is $2y^2-x^2=2$ which is a hyperbola.\n\nSo, only statements II and III are true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124288 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124476 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "dfd8982d-d859-5eb2-9f35-69af39c04822" :knowledge-point/title "Sketching Level Curves"}] :question/id #uuid "618e7097-38d3-5167-a9d2-5d5a3fc85e0a" :question/math-academy-id "e-4229" :question/problem "Sketch the level curves of the surface $z=e^{x^2-y^2}.$" :question/worked-solution "The level curves for the function $f(x,y)=e^{x^2-y^2}$ take the form\n\n$$\ne^{x^2-y^2} = c.\n$$\n\nNote that we must have the constraint $c\\gt 0$ since $e^x \\gt 0$ for all $x.$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}=c \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}})=\\operatorname{ln}⁡c \\\\ {x}^{2}-{y}^{2}=\\operatorname{ln}⁡c.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can split this into three cases, depending on the sign of $\\ln c.$\n\n- Case 1: $\\ln c \\gt 0.$ In this case, we have the family of hyperbolas $x^2-y^2 = \\ln c.$\n\n- Case 2: $\\ln c = 0.$ In this case, we have the lines $y=\\pm x.$\n\n- Case 3: $\\ln c < 0.$ In this case, we have the family of hyperbolas $y^2 - x^2 = -\\ln c.$\n\nTherefore, the level curves are as follows:\n\n![](images/5f/5f2ec43639cb31e03cc4a00e43969c7f0333c098fc4b366ea1609772faabfda5.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124362 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124553 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "62dff73b-1857-5192-ae10-fe22577cbfb4" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Equation of a Level Curve"}] :question/id #uuid "fe87d9e4-6445-5ee7-9dc7-6ab8fbb165c3" :question/math-academy-id "e-5968" :question/problem "Find the equation of the level curve that passes through the point $G\\big(\\sqrt{5}, 1\\big)$ for the function $f(x,y) = \\dfrac{12y}{x^2-y^2}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the value of the function at $G$:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n  f\\big(\\sqrt{5}, 1\\big)&= \\dfrac{12(1)}{\\big(\\sqrt{5}\\big)^2 - 1^2} = 3}\n$$\n\nHence, the level curve that passes through $G\\big(\\sqrt{5}, 1\\big)$ is the $3$-level curve.\n\nRecall that the level curves for the function $f(x,y)$ are given by the equation\n\n$$\nf(x,y) = c.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we're interested in $c=3.$ So, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & =c \\\\ \\frac{12y}{{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}} & =3 \\\\ 4y & ={x}^{2}-{y}^{2} \\\\ {x}^{2}-{y}^{2}-4y-4 & =-4 \\\\ {x}^{2}-({y}^{2}+4y+4) & =-4 \\\\ {x}^{2}-(y+2)^{2} & =-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the level curve that passes through $G\\big(\\sqrt{5}, 1\\big)$ is the hyperbola $x^2 - (y+2)^2 = -4.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186378559 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124553 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "62dff73b-1857-5192-ae10-fe22577cbfb4" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Equation of a Level Curve"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "995200e2-5e10-52e1-90be-fc815f544450" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=1-y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378561} {:answer/id #uuid "ae5d37a2-e3f4-52f8-88c7-9baa4e8494ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=2{y}^{2}+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378562} {:answer/id #uuid "09235770-a24c-5100-9f0f-3f63222ce061" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x={y}^{2}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378563} {:answer/id #uuid "c24e2c48-252f-55d1-b420-84ec94b43128" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=2y-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378564} {:answer/id #uuid "d9ffc8e1-87ad-5ae1-a981-54948903b3a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x={y}^{2}-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378565}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ae5d37a2-e3f4-52f8-88c7-9baa4e8494ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=2{y}^{2}+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378562} :answer-field/id #uuid "4491bbbe-7549-50e8-ad8a-aca200ce17e3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378560}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8f75e12b-5e13-5df3-af5b-158f6f119451" :question/math-academy-id "q-128446" :question/problem "What is the equation of the level curve that passes through the point $P(3,-1)$ for the function $f(x,y)=\\frac{x}{2{y}^{2}+1}?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the value of the function at $P:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(3,-1) & =\\frac{3}{2(-1)^{2}+1} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2+1} \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the level curve that passes through $P(3,-1)$ is the $1$-level curve.\n\nRecall that the level curves for the function $f(x,y)$ are given by the equation\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=c.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we're interested in $c=1.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & =c \\\\ \\frac{x}{2{y}^{2}+1} & =1 \\\\ x & =2{y}^{2}+1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the level curve that passes through $P(3,-1)$ is the parabola $x=2{y}^{2}+1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186436027 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124553 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "62dff73b-1857-5192-ae10-fe22577cbfb4" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Equation of a Level Curve"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0329b153-bf57-5eea-8e4f-f3f01337857b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=3-2x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436009} {:answer/id #uuid "44caf6b5-57f9-522a-a950-aba744b9e3c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-\\frac{1}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436012} {:answer/id #uuid "6d6f7295-9d6c-517b-9e6e-6ee1b2c02c7e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{2}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436013} {:answer/id #uuid "9a0b0721-1fd0-5994-a36a-82e40db9769c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=x-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436015} {:answer/id #uuid "cc8a8126-4229-53cd-bece-781ab226e64b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=2-x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436018}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9a0b0721-1fd0-5994-a36a-82e40db9769c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=x-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436015} :answer-field/id #uuid "11ea0465-98a8-532d-bb2d-293a976cf74c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436023}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "af624627-f936-5c7e-a5ee-772c5d7da48f" :question/math-academy-id "q-128448" :question/problem "What is the equation of the level curve that passes through the point $P(3,-1)$ for the function $f(x,y)=\\frac{2}{x-y}?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the value of the function at $P:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(3,-1) & =\\frac{2}{3-(-1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3+1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the level curve that passes through $P(3,-1)$ is the $\\frac{1}{2}$-level curve.\n\nRecall that the level curves for the function $f(x,y)$ are given by the equation\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=c.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we're interested in $c=\\frac{1}{2}.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & =c \\\\ \\frac{2}{x-y} & =\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 4 & =x-y \\\\ y & =x-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the level curve that passes through $P(3,-1)$ is the line $y=x-4.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186436026 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124553 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "62dff73b-1857-5192-ae10-fe22577cbfb4" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Equation of a Level Curve"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "000302c2-3c84-5577-bb85-c11cc3bf9cee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4{x}^{2}+9{y}^{2}=25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436008} {:answer/id #uuid "0bb60a10-e100-54a3-a098-70fb2ea763e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4{x}^{2}+9{y}^{2}=36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436010} {:answer/id #uuid "6df11da8-be9b-5344-b62d-79a4559efa3c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9{x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}=36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436014} {:answer/id #uuid "a513aedd-cbc7-5326-bb5e-498f3f229294" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9{x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}=25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436016} {:answer/id #uuid "df1cdfb6-d415-5196-8163-5b0778c79a74" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9{x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}=16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436020}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "000302c2-3c84-5577-bb85-c11cc3bf9cee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4{x}^{2}+9{y}^{2}=25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436008} :answer-field/id #uuid "30fcae88-a1e2-5970-b696-299270bb46fe" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436024}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "563f43ed-8e03-5890-8ba0-fe3a95b9c80d" :question/math-academy-id "q-128450" :question/problem "What is the equation of the level curve that passes through the point $P(-2,-1)$ for the function $f(x,y)=4{x}^{2}+9{y}^{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the value of the function at $P:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-2,-1) & =4{(-2)}^{2}+9{(-1)}^{2} \\\\  & =4(4)+9(1) \\\\  & =16+9 \\\\  & =25\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the level curve that passes through $P(-2,-1)$ is the $25$-level curve.\n\nRecall that the level curves for the function $f(x,y)$ are given by the equation\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=c.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we're interested in $c=25.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & =c \\\\ 4{x}^{2}+9{y}^{2} & =25\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the level curve that passes through $P(-2,-1)$ is the ellipse $4{x}^{2}+9{y}^{2}=25.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262933 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124475 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "74f126da-5f3b-5af8-9aee-d6f0a4c61c49" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Shape of a Level Curve"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "026909dc-e9dd-517f-95bf-6823f8e3bc01" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259892} {:answer/id #uuid "38140770-9691-5eb2-ad82-564a6f9d48cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260373} {:answer/id #uuid "48b9e9d1-a24c-55df-b4fb-a8d5b1fad5e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260505} {:answer/id #uuid "5c7319ce-b6b6-5eaa-8243-6ea4d88a73fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260665} {:answer/id #uuid "77e909ae-017b-58b1-aa6e-edb4e7831d28" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260923}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "48b9e9d1-a24c-55df-b4fb-a8d5b1fad5e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260505} :answer-field/id #uuid "576917ef-8805-5f21-a670-caf9478ceb93" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262272}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "02aab097-5368-5094-843f-c0ac47beef5b" :question/math-academy-id "q-129058" :question/problem "The level curves of the function $f(x,y)=\\frac{x+{y}^{2}}{x}$ are given by $f(x,y)=c.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $c=-1$ gives a line\n\nII. $c=0$ gives a parabola, excluding the origin\n\nIII. $c=1$ gives the $x$-axis, excluding the origin" :question/worked-solution "Setting $f(x,y)=c$ gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x+{y}^{2}}{x} & =c \\\\ x+{y}^{2} & =cx \\\\ x(1-c)+{y}^{2} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore:\n\n- If $c=-1,$ the level curve is $x=-\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{2},$ which is a parabola that opens to the left (excluding the origin). So, I is false.\n\n- If $c=0,$ the level curves is $x=-{y}^{2},$ which is a parabola that opens to the left (excluding the origin). So, II is true.\n\n- If $c=1,$ the level curve is $y=0,$ which is the $x$-axis (excluding the origin). So, III is true.\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"II and III only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186387978 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124476 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "dfd8982d-d859-5eb2-9f35-69af39c04822" :knowledge-point/title "Sketching Level Curves"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7c206d91-b8f5-5a94-9316-75270a63bcd8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/c2/c2c7ac29fce22a4448d286307dd3a87839c413f0a422cbdc2dbd13dc04144a7b.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387980} {:answer/id #uuid "93f2eb5a-6350-5c8e-9435-c85bdfe64e00" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/8a/8a631f2285c079c2effd4aea2c80fcf2f250a2c96f6ab11ca5b79961de5c3ce3.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387981} {:answer/id #uuid "277bab86-7c6e-508e-9834-448c0cb1c29b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/7a/7aa8f113ff110ff76dba8a4bbb75eed0e3368c46a82eed25c00d63498c56f822.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387982} {:answer/id #uuid "b8bb77ca-8f07-5dac-beec-6bf48ca04c32" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/74/74db591aa317d90939685ef8a9f73c109c233b3f0f0cba971920ba4fcb1b4854.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387983} {:answer/id #uuid "f9fe9eb1-102d-5d7f-9c07-0688f68ddc05" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/91/91fde8bc9eb57c1974e622a6673a030c9889c77d6788b620ffe70d7d6a8409c5.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387984}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f9fe9eb1-102d-5d7f-9c07-0688f68ddc05" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/91/91fde8bc9eb57c1974e622a6673a030c9889c77d6788b620ffe70d7d6a8409c5.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387984} :answer-field/id #uuid "8a1b305a-d716-5bd9-a834-19012dc96cc0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387979}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e75a1d08-2fa1-51fa-b251-a3f4ae4ef9d8" :question/math-academy-id "q-129112" :question/problem "Which of the following represents the level curves of $f(x,y)=y-x?$" :question/worked-solution "The level curves for the function $f(x,y)$ are given by the equations \n\n$$\nf(x,y)=c.\n$$\n\nNotice that the range of $f(x,y)$ is $(-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ So, we will consider level curves for any value of $c.$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & =c \\\\ y-x & =c \\\\ y & =x+c.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation above gives us a family of lines with slope of $1.$ Therefore, the correct graph is as follows:\n\n![](images/91/91fde8bc9eb57c1974e622a6673a030c9889c77d6788b620ffe70d7d6a8409c5.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186436028 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124476 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "dfd8982d-d859-5eb2-9f35-69af39c04822" :knowledge-point/title "Sketching Level Curves"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "19118c24-d5da-5954-9e93-75cfa8bacbe5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/3c/3c44ae1b59af6ac6f64efedcf4242aaad07ddcf98c2b63c4aeae7958a6622874.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436011} {:answer/id #uuid "b68c227f-79b4-539e-9f21-17aa72aae1be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/3f/3fde41d8d88f0d843e80ae813b07ec030502bcbaa060bc5d54ade4f5207a8740.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436017} {:answer/id #uuid "d4fdc308-acd9-599d-98f4-61b51923dcf4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/ca/ca10c21bb658bc3075d0d66321d888c2b23596c1416f605ab0bb8cf79c40af24.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436019} {:answer/id #uuid "ea4ea415-1a42-5ab9-a4f6-74d5d9c47e2c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/08/0857b5d843c6d3f5ca6218ee0f27fe169aedc59676b245578bc8db21fabe6178.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436021} {:answer/id #uuid "f049c9a7-cc49-5c3f-a4df-0714b2f9933a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/c6/c6a799db8c86ff2bfb702dbba92f8d26011d33016aa33f5df1b4a58601205f04.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436022}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "19118c24-d5da-5954-9e93-75cfa8bacbe5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/3c/3c44ae1b59af6ac6f64efedcf4242aaad07ddcf98c2b63c4aeae7958a6622874.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436011} :answer-field/id #uuid "adf8aa6a-75ee-5eec-b556-6b1e3d610f4a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436025}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "c5ccf563-8a57-5f1f-ad06-ef72dc726ab7" :question/math-academy-id "q-129114" :question/problem "Which of the following represents the level curves of $f(x,y)={y}^{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that the range of $f(x,y)$ is $[0,\\infty ).$ So, we will consider only $c$-level curves for $c\\ge 0.$\n\nThe level curves for the function $f(x,y)$ are given by the equations \n\n$$\nf(x,y)=c.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & =c \\\\ {y}^{2} & =c \\\\ y & =\\pm \\sqrt{c}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that the equations $y=\\pm \\sqrt{c}$ do not depend on $x.$ So, for a given $c\\in [0,\\infty ),$ the right-hand side of the equation is constant. As a result, we obtain a family of horizontal lines, as shown below.\n\n![](images/3c/3c44ae1b59af6ac6f64efedcf4242aaad07ddcf98c2b63c4aeae7958a6622874.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186387992 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124476 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "dfd8982d-d859-5eb2-9f35-69af39c04822" :knowledge-point/title "Sketching Level Curves"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "69ffca37-cace-5fde-98f2-279fdf4f3975" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/56/56e923e4c1e2603c9bd3c621df0a5a4043fcc6a37ac73427be14541407fc19d8.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387994} {:answer/id #uuid "9ef1d420-a12a-56ca-a25f-8624b9640b47" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/09/09f1a18e1a6fdcd29a40026cbffd8e8bdec23511bb692a1e920c18f942042470.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387995} {:answer/id #uuid "6719fa96-fc32-59ff-ad37-8586f87f620f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/67/67e9cfee7779fdde389a0804e7f52372ca9434de56b6611d296d4ac9c0759f72.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387996} {:answer/id #uuid "2c7de16e-8fae-51b2-b167-c594ccf39873" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/aa/aa4d0cd189808c717648640c5543a632c099970a19d38d44298d409054f2627c.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387997} {:answer/id #uuid "3995e781-cbde-5cfd-b61f-9c376d6d3f49" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/bf/bf0f4b592cde648f63b21523aba1a49aeeb3b4dcaf909ba72c4629e088ca372a.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387998}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6719fa96-fc32-59ff-ad37-8586f87f620f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/67/67e9cfee7779fdde389a0804e7f52372ca9434de56b6611d296d4ac9c0759f72.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387996} :answer-field/id #uuid "5053c438-eb23-5e9c-bd54-db15189721dc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387993}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "9ec437fa-7d05-53d2-8259-19727f28f519" :question/math-academy-id "q-129117" :question/problem "![](images/03/037422e7b1ce3b3d9067aba39c4fa85c6311770e63e70758c34aa61629c7f58e.png)\n\nWhich of the following could represent the level curves of the surface $z=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡y$ shown above?" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that the range of $f(x,y)$ is $[-1,1].$ So, we will consider only $c$-level curves for $c\\in [-1,1].$\n\nThe level curves for the function $f(x,y)$ are given by the equations \n\n$$\nf(x,y)=c.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & =c \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡y & =c \\\\ y & =-\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡c+2\\pi n,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ can be any integer. \n\nNotice that the equations $y=-\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡c+2\\pi n$ do not depend on $x.$ So, for a given $c\\in [-1,1]$ and integer $n$, the right-hand side of the equation is constant. As a result, we obtain a family of horizontal lines, as shown below.\n\n![](images/67/67e9cfee7779fdde389a0804e7f52372ca9434de56b6611d296d4ac9c0759f72.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186402427 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124475 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "74f126da-5f3b-5af8-9aee-d6f0a4c61c49" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Shape of a Level Curve"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4ccd00e2-e51e-5254-b333-5c31e7370efa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402429} {:answer/id #uuid "e79d828e-64db-52fa-a52e-0190594eb1d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402430} {:answer/id #uuid "b8b008e1-d401-59be-bfbd-56ed2924d87f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402431} {:answer/id #uuid "1746a306-b5b0-58c3-9e66-12d72428be02" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402432} {:answer/id #uuid "c67ed439-b900-57c4-ac4d-543a0744030c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402433}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e79d828e-64db-52fa-a52e-0190594eb1d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402430} :answer-field/id #uuid "483ba923-28c4-52eb-887b-56bdd19045ab" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402428}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "fb8b2d04-67d4-51d3-8ebf-71fc804b1a61" :question/math-academy-id "q-35527" :question/problem "The level curves of the function $f(x,y)=xy$ are given by $f(x,y)=c.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $c=1$ gives a hyperbola\n\nII. $c=-1$ gives a parabola\n\nIII. $c=0$ gives the axes $x=0$ and $y=0$" :question/worked-solution "Setting $f(x,y)=c$ gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}xy & =c\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore:\n\n- If $c=\\pm 1$ then the level curves are $xy=\\pm 1,$ which are hyperbolas.\n\n- If $c=0$ then the level curves are $xy=0,$ which consists of the axes $x=0$ and $y=0.$\n\nSo, only statements I and III are true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124890 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124475 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "74f126da-5f3b-5af8-9aee-d6f0a4c61c49" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Shape of a Level Curve"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fa10b2ad-a1b5-5256-bd41-d9d81726811a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379761} {:answer/id #uuid "4a49deeb-c270-5080-857d-8612168a0bbc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379762} {:answer/id #uuid "b5d243fd-f2bf-5324-b8c2-1d4dfe9211ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379763} {:answer/id #uuid "8c0d4795-c2f6-5544-933a-f27e852880cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379764} {:answer/id #uuid "b706b1a1-a4d4-59fc-ba44-34813a322035" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379765}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4a49deeb-c270-5080-857d-8612168a0bbc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379762} :answer-field/id #uuid "6fc98371-9305-5542-adef-51d5a2f11dd5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379760}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b428de76-1b52-5416-9b1c-9157ab5ea778" :question/math-academy-id "q-35534" :question/problem "The level curves of the function $f(x,y)=\\frac{2{x}^{2}+1}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}$ are given by $f(x,y)=c.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $c=1$ gives a hyperbola\n\nII. $c=2$ gives a parabola\n\nIII. $c=3$ gives an ellipse" :question/worked-solution "Setting $f(x,y)=c$ gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2{x}^{2}+1}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} & =c \\\\ 2{x}^{2}+1 & =c({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}) \\\\ (c-2){x}^{2}+c{y}^{2} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore:\n\n- If $c=1$ then the level curve is ${y}^{2}-{x}^{2}=1,$ which is a hyperbola.\n\n- If $c=2$ then the level curves are $y=\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2},$ which consists of two lines.\n\n- If $c=3$ then the level curve is ${x}^{2}+3{y}^{2}=1,$ which is an ellipse.\n\nSo, only statements I and III are true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125014 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124475 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "74f126da-5f3b-5af8-9aee-d6f0a4c61c49" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Shape of a Level Curve"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ca9aedb9-5c6e-5ab9-b703-822e9744cd18" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122685} {:answer/id #uuid "dd17347f-22ff-571f-a6d7-807b93a366b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122686} {:answer/id #uuid "18531f6c-e1f0-5729-80f5-92a693529d56" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122687} {:answer/id #uuid "1ea134b6-4449-59bd-be9f-503cfe8288e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122688} {:answer/id #uuid "6d0a480c-dbb2-5e27-a839-546a7c305a98" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122689}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "18531f6c-e1f0-5729-80f5-92a693529d56" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122687} :answer-field/id #uuid "89f9deee-f7c4-5ce2-84fc-017b6026db36" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122684}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "592215bc-9340-546e-9e8f-8c90c87cd2d2" :question/math-academy-id "q-36829" :question/problem "The level curves of the function $f(x,y)={x}^{3}y-{y}^{2}x$ are given by $f(x,y)=c.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $c=-1$ gives a line\n\nII. $c=0$ gives a parabola and the axes $x=0$ and $y=0$\n\nIII. $c=1$ gives two lines" :question/worked-solution "Setting $f(x,y)=c$ gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{3}y-{y}^{2}x & =c \\\\ xy({x}^{2}-y) & =c\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore:\n\n- If $c=\\pm 1$ then the level curves are $xy({x}^{2}-y)=\\pm 1,$ which are not lines.\n\n- If $c=0$ then the level curves are $xy({x}^{2}-y)=0,$ which consists of the axes $x=0$ and $y=0$, and the parabola $y={x}^{2}.$\n\nSo, only statement II is true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125179 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124476 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "dfd8982d-d859-5eb2-9f35-69af39c04822" :knowledge-point/title "Sketching Level Curves"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0fbb4807-24a9-5fa7-a053-64ede7706481" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/79/79d8db55b0de544c328188d2af444d848658b65626e753bdc1654791cc457506.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333129} {:answer/id #uuid "6510be84-880e-5d4f-804e-c57c775526c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/6f/6f16e785aaef98bf6609a4ef79b6574e3650110607680da5fdbb8034eb590457.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333908} {:answer/id #uuid "9a1f5f69-600f-50ee-bca5-b6a75b2877f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/65/6521da99a82e38a68a5aa87a0c7c88eacf4ed7b78351af594ec309fa2cb7f57b.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334350} {:answer/id #uuid "b785490c-3fb9-5a57-894e-b521694b263e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/56/56e4941d265e1fc778e7b5672a14f38d45ba43b13562f3ddab53cebd5175cea4.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334597} {:answer/id #uuid "d906d727-e913-509d-9cf4-4581970726ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/4c/4c259d100b5e63a37822df6f7a5b5a6493efdb13b147a76a0183d120e6aeec5b.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334893}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9a1f5f69-600f-50ee-bca5-b6a75b2877f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/65/6521da99a82e38a68a5aa87a0c7c88eacf4ed7b78351af594ec309fa2cb7f57b.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334350} :answer-field/id #uuid "49202a10-c9c8-5356-be37-70bc7b8b058d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335383}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5348f454-8724-5136-a5f0-8c87b0d92c2a" :question/math-academy-id "q-64908" :question/problem "Which of the following represents the level curves of $f(x,y)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(y-2{x}^{2})?$" :question/worked-solution "The level curves for the function $f(x,y)$ are given by the equations \n\n$$\nf(x,y)=c.\n$$\n\nNotice that the range of $f(x,y)$ is $(-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ So, we will consider level curves for any value of $c.$\n\nTherefore, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & =c \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(y-2{x}^{2}) & =c \\\\ y-2{x}^{2} & ={e}^{c} \\\\ y & =2{x}^{2}+{e}^{c}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation above gives us a family of parabolas with the vertex at $(0,{e}^{c}).$ Therefore, the correct graph is as follows:\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\n![](images/65/6521da99a82e38a68a5aa87a0c7c88eacf4ed7b78351af594ec309fa2cb7f57b.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186379896 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124553 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "62dff73b-1857-5192-ae10-fe22577cbfb4" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Equation of a Level Curve"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8a86f79f-60fc-5217-9c6b-a03f33f604de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}-2{y}^{2}=20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379898} {:answer/id #uuid "908be2b8-6e9b-571a-8f86-e456deb80232" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{x}^{2}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}=20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379899} {:answer/id #uuid "8cd8e1a5-58ec-5407-b39e-0663ce69ce38" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}=20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379900} {:answer/id #uuid "475201b1-53d3-5bd4-b0f0-119e6038ce74" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{x}^{2}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}=20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379901} {:answer/id #uuid "94ca828d-54b6-5990-afc7-c4497e745042" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+2{y}^{2}=20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379902}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "94ca828d-54b6-5990-afc7-c4497e745042" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+2{y}^{2}=20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379902} :answer-field/id #uuid "bc0fc72b-f01f-5a55-9f63-17e0f1879f6f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379897}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "769b357f-4fb6-5958-a803-d881c01aed36" :question/math-academy-id "q-71201" :question/problem "Find the equation of the level curve that passes through the point $M(2,3)$ for the function $f(x,y)=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+2{y}^{2}-15.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the value of the function at $M$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(2,3) & =\\frac{{2}^{2}}{2}+2(3)^{2}-15=5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the level curve that passes through $M(2,3)$ is the $5$-level curve.\n\nRecall that the level curves for the function $f(x,y)$ are given by the equation\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=c.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we're interested in $c=5.$ So, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & =c \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+2{y}^{2}-15 & =5 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+2{y}^{2} & =20\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the level curve that passes through $M(2,3)$ is the ellipse $\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+2{y}^{2}=20.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338915 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124553 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "62dff73b-1857-5192-ae10-fe22577cbfb4" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Equation of a Level Curve"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "379edbc4-958b-59eb-bdc5-5897f81d1e31" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y-2=4{x}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336550} {:answer/id #uuid "3bbf9aff-6ec4-5ead-8cb9-70f1e2c12474" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336594} {:answer/id #uuid "93f41eb2-bc74-558f-a139-bec3b72aa513" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}+(y-2)^{2}=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337384} {:answer/id #uuid "e68d2210-b853-5c64-a844-85c31e696235" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(y-2)^{2}-{x}^{2}=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338045} {:answer/id #uuid "e88e5fd5-cf85-57c8-b1a6-37efdcf80aac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4x=\\pm (y-2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338062}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "93f41eb2-bc74-558f-a139-bec3b72aa513" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}+(y-2)^{2}=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337384} :answer-field/id #uuid "0b1487de-32bb-570f-8c7f-10e1855abb71" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338296}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "bb2a5bfe-54ec-5329-9de1-bfb5261e1c81" :question/math-academy-id "q-71213" :question/problem "Find the equation of the level curve that passes through the point $V(2,2)$ for the function $f(x,y)=\\frac{8y}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the value of the function at $V$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(2,2) & =\\frac{8(2)}{{2}^{2}+{2}^{2}}=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the level curve that passes through $V(2,2)$ is the $2$-level curve.\n\nRecall that the level curves for the function $f(x,y)$ are given by the equation\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=c.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we're interested in $c=2.$ So, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & =c \\\\ \\frac{8y}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} & =2 \\\\ 4y & ={x}^{2}+{y}^{2} \\\\ {x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-4y+4 & =4 \\\\ {x}^{2}+(y-2)^{2} & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the level curve that passes through $V(2,2)$ is the circle ${x}^{2}+(y-2)^{2}=4.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338937 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124475 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "74f126da-5f3b-5af8-9aee-d6f0a4c61c49" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Shape of a Level Curve"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a905dcc-7062-5ba9-9481-732d5b5264b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336131} {:answer/id #uuid "92663878-d31f-5b9a-82dc-e0531f783d7c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337363} {:answer/id #uuid "9e18aeef-f61b-5c4d-a0f7-d57397008dc9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337462} {:answer/id #uuid "a5ece99e-e9d1-5800-b5d5-2a569fbee7c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337538} {:answer/id #uuid "c045c018-7da4-5278-a1f9-dc81aff7cf6b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337739}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "92663878-d31f-5b9a-82dc-e0531f783d7c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337363} :answer-field/id #uuid "c4f5ebcf-28da-59c5-ae3f-90358c258495" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338631}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b94a6f8a-60a9-5806-9e18-4814d39c5835" :question/math-academy-id "q-71395" :question/problem "The level curves of the function $f(x,y)=\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-2{y}^{2}}$ are given by $f(x,y)=c.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $c=1$ gives a line\n\nII. $c=2$ gives a hyperbola\n\nIII. $c=0$ gives two lines" :question/worked-solution "Setting $f(x,y)=c$ gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-2{y}^{2}} & =c \\\\ {x}^{2}-2{y}^{2} & ={c}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore:\n\n- If $c=1$ then the level curve is ${x}^{2}-2{y}^{2}=1,$ which is not a line.\n\n- If $c=2$ then the level curve is ${x}^{2}-2{y}^{2}=4,$ which is a hyperbola.\n\n- If $c=0$ then the level curve is $y=\\pm \\frac{x}{\\sqrt{2}},$ which consists of two lines.\n\nSo, only statements II and III are true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186393140 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124476 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "dfd8982d-d859-5eb2-9f35-69af39c04822" :knowledge-point/title "Sketching Level Curves"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bdd6b5d4-ea23-5caf-8777-7138860af8ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/98/98d449048718ab75fc54a659bc74314f26b6059c5e7a7ed4af28b7edfeb69a69.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393142} {:answer/id #uuid "7487cd45-f801-550a-a1b4-5e2864c83b4b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/a8/a8c4e910e3884ee68518752ab814f491edb14d422b4c25926b7d3ad34720592d.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393143} {:answer/id #uuid "2bc74059-a769-52e2-bcbf-ddccb68efbb2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/c5/c5ea7e325483eeb3572c90b78a5cf72040d84b98dee51a1ca2bdf4dcab5b8d2f.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393144} {:answer/id #uuid "7fd43447-80cf-50a5-8942-6f1234cad571" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/d7/d7569d1df433554420caf9b30c06a3baf6fc73c150bf41e898e7c66333946553.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393145} {:answer/id #uuid "4cbca4ce-0d9a-5eff-be43-6a0f899caae9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/f3/f33a74f9c61703628cd53576dc12b8a02d67944dccd70e3ea6d1be88ba3fa5d8.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393146}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2bc74059-a769-52e2-bcbf-ddccb68efbb2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/c5/c5ea7e325483eeb3572c90b78a5cf72040d84b98dee51a1ca2bdf4dcab5b8d2f.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393144} :answer-field/id #uuid "077949f5-62c8-59b7-9b63-c9e8b3537b15" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393141}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "d3f898f6-b08f-5687-adf4-0ea719bca50f" :question/math-academy-id "q-71413" :question/problem "![](images/29/29253192bb8863030c3464dd2c42be40922db96f3de6f3e57674f2a59f862e09.png)\n\nWhich of the following could represent the level curves of the surface $z=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ shown above?" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that the range of $f(x,y)$ is $[-1,1].$ So, we will consider only $c$-level curves for $c\\in [-1,1].$\n\nThe level curves for the function $f(x,y)$ are given by the equations \n\n$$\nf(x,y)=c\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & =c \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡x & =c \\\\ x & =\\pm \\operatorname{arccos}⁡c+2\\pi n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ can be any integer. \n\nNotice that in the equations $x=\\pm \\operatorname{arccos}⁡c+2\\pi n$ do not depend on $y.$ So, for a given $c\\in [-1,1]$ and integer $n$, the right-hand side of the equation is constant. As a result, we obtain a family of vertical lines, as shown below.\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\n![](images/c5/c5ea7e325483eeb3572c90b78a5cf72040d84b98dee51a1ca2bdf4dcab5b8d2f.png)"}]}
